"""Generate the human-readable ledger from the mastered asset manifest."""
import pathlib,json
root=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
data=json.loads((root/'app/src/main/assets/audio-manifest.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
lines=['# Bundled recordings and licenses','','Updated 10 November 2026. Five source recordings were downloaded through Pixabay\'s public browser controls and mastered offline into six interactive effects. The app no longer depends on reaching Freesound.','','## Sound matches','','| Effect | Author | Licensed source | Match and edits |','|---|---|---|---|']
for name,m in data.items():
    if name.startswith('_'):continue
    lines.append(f"| {name} | {m['author']} | [{m['source_filename']}]({m['source']}) | {m['match_status']} |")
lines+=['','## License and use','','All adopted recordings are used under the [Pixabay Content License](https://pixabay.com/service/terms/), terms version dated 20 October 2026, inspected in the browser on 10 November 2026. They are **not represented as CC0**. Audio is combined with original illustrations, particles, camera input, controls and authored timelines in this app. Do not redistribute these files as a standalone sound library. Original downloaded MP3s remain in ignored `.research/audio-inputs/`; they are not part of the source distribution. Some Pixabay entries are published by its freesound_community account, with original artists credited above; acquisition and license verification took place on Pixabay, without accessing the blocked Freesound origin.','','The original artwork and Kotlin code have no claim of ownership over these recordings. Full credits and source links are available inside Options → Sound credits.','','## Mastering and provenance','','Every output is 48 kHz mono PCM16. Gain is adjusted conservatively; pitch is unchanged. Clip edges use 10 ms fades and each track ends in 250 ms silence. A one-second excerpt of real sparkler hiss (oneSparkler, source seconds 16–17) supplies a virtual ignition cue; this is not claimed as an actual fuse recording.','','Anar uses the fountain recording. Phuljhadi uses source seconds 34–48.1 of oneSparkler. Chakri uses the complete spinning-bee recording. Sky shot uses the complete explosion-with-echo recording, with ascent aligned to the lead-in. Sutli isolates source seconds 10.9–11.6 of CRACKER SOUND; its specific subtype is unverified. Ladi is an authored sequence of 36 pops extracted from the Diwali field recording; exact excerpt offsets and output timings are recorded in the manifest. It is not an untouched ladi field recording.','','`app/src/main/assets/audio-manifest.json` is the precise machine-readable ledger: source URLs, file names, source/output SHA-256 hashes, trim boundaries, gain, cue times, ladi assembly edits and match limitations. The preparation script performs no network requests.','','## Output checksums','','| File | Duration | SHA-256 |','|---|---|---|']
for name,m in data.items():
    if not name.startswith('_'):lines.append(f"| audio/{name}.wav | {m['duration']:.3f} s | `{m['sha256']}` |")
lines+=['','## Original artwork','','The six tray illustrations, app icon, placement reticle and particle graphics are original programmatic artwork. The user\'s reference photographs establish the categories; branded packaging and logos are not copied.','','## Review limits','','Source descriptions and waveforms were inspected; a physical listening/fidelity review and Poco M5 audiovisual timing review remain required. These are authentic recording excerpts and edited sequences, with the subtype limitations above. No claim of exact branded-product reproduction is made. The independent OpenGameArt CC0 pack investigated during sourcing was not adopted and is not bundled.']
(root/'ASSETS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
print('Updated ASSETS.md')
